artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $V = \bigoplus_{n\geq 0} V_n$ be a vertex operator algebra over $\mathbb{C}$ satisfying the following three conditions:

(1) the central charge of $V$ equals $24$;
(2) $V_1 = 0$, i.e., $V$ has no nonzero elements of conformal weight $1$;
(3) every irreducible $V$-module is isomorphic to $V$ itself, and every $V$-module is completely reducible (so $V$ is holomorphic/self-dual and rational).

Prove or disprove: any such $V$ must be isomorphic, as a vertex operator algebra, to the moonshine module vertex operator algebra $V^{\natural}$ constructed by Frenkel–Lepowsky–Meurman.

